Reason: a tile_add copied the room's whole tile array to make room for one more tile, and every tile_add or
tile_delete marked the id index stale, so the next tile lookup rebuilt it over every tile. In rm_a3h04 each crumbling
sand block makes its neighbours delete and re-add their edge tiles, alternating tile_exists and tile_delete, so a
single crumble rebuilt the ~3,000-entry index dozens of times; with Samus falling through the sand the room ran at
about 20 fps on the real Wii. The tile array now grows by half again when it is full, and tile_add and tile_delete
keep a current index up to date (a delete re-points only the tiles after the one removed). A lookup still confirms
each hit against the array and falls back to the walk on any miss, as before.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

